<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολί̄τ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιήτης</span></b>  (q.v.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>citizen, freeman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.558
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22.429
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.131
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				5.16
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀγαθός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.42
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				517c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					271
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεως, πόλεων π.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ γᾶς πατρίας πολῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					806
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὁρίζεται τῷ μετέχειν κρίσεως καὶ
					ἀρχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1275a22
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
			<i>fellow-citizen</i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιήτης</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1.14
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάδμου π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθηναίων π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.139
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					20.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					339e
				</span></i>
			: and by a Com. metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴνου π. ὢν κρατίστου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Amphis
					36
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<i>belonging to, connected with one's city</i> or <i>country,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοὶ πολῖται,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολιοῦχοι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				253
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δῆμος,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τῆς πόλεως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				574
			</span></i>.</div>
